  "name": "Black Mist — Cinematic Diffusion",
  "description": "Black Mist / Black Pro-Mist-inspired photographic diffusion. A graduated highlight extractor retains luminous source strength even at high Highlight Threshold values; a normalized 16-tap, four-radius bilinear scattering kernel spreads their colour to nearby pixels. Bloom adds light around highlights without subtracting their bright cores, avoiding dark edge halos. Fine Detail Softness blends a larger two-scale blur while protecting prominent edges. Diffusion Density scales scattering and detail softness; Scatter Strength adjusts bloom transfer; Bloom Radius is measured in pixels at a 1080px short edge; Wide Halo adds the distant tail; Halo Warmth, Shadow Lift, Highlight Compression and Effect Mix complete the grade. A stateless, single-pass approximation, not a calibrated optical diffusion measurement or true Gaussian PSF. At maximum settings isolated light sources may show faint sampling directions; use on opaque photos. Defaults favour a clearly visible, moderate cinematic diffusion treatment.",
